{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U1", "R5"],
      "pins": ["U1.8", "R5.1", "R5.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "ESP32-C3-MINI-1 U1 pin 8, named EN/CHIP_PU, is connected directly to the GND net. R5, a 10k resistor, is connected between +3V3 and GND rather than to the EN pin.",
      "expected": "The MCU must be enabled for the CF-Chef controller firmware to run; EN/CHIP_PU should be pulled high to +3V3, or otherwise driven high, not tied directly to GND. The specification lists R5 as one of the pull-up/pull-down resistors associated with strapping/EN/fan-tach.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"13\") (name \"GND\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"8\") (pinfunction \"EN/CHIP_PU\") (pintype \"input\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R5 0 +3V3 10k"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "`+3V3` net feeds: ESP32 (`U1` pin 3, `3V3`), the three MAX31855 thermocouple ICs (`U2`/`U3`/`U4` pin 4, `V_{CC}`), the WS2812B status LED (`D1` `VDD`), decoupling caps `C3/C4/C6/C8/C9/C10/C12`, and pull-up/pull-down resistors `R2/R5/R6/R11` (strapping/EN/fan-tach related — see MCU/thermocouple sections)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The ESP32-C3 is held in reset/disabled, so the board cannot boot firmware, read thermocouples, control the heater, monitor fans, or provide Wi-Fi/status functions.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["C7"],
      "pins": ["C7.1", "C7.2"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The 10uF capacitor C7 has both pins on the GND net; C7 pin 1 and C7 pin 2 are both connected to GND.",
      "expected": "A 10uF capacitor in the MCU/3.3V supply area should connect two distinct nets, most plausibly +3V3 and GND, to provide decoupling or bulk supply capacitance. A capacitor with both terminals on the same net is functionally shorted across itself and does not decouple the rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C7\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C7\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C7 0 0 10u"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "C7 provides no decoupling as connected. If it was intended as bulk 3.3V capacitance, the supply rail loses that capacitance and may be less stable or noisier.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build contains a major connectivity deviation: the ESP32-C3 EN/CHIP_PU pin is shorted to GND and the associated pull-up resistor R5 is tied between +3V3 and GND, which would disable the MCU. A secondary likely error is C7, a 10uF capacitor with both terminals on GND, leaving it functionally unused."
}

